Quoting   <cheepicus@hotmail.com>:
>* Diminishing returns on negative AC.
>Leaning towards: DR = min(min(rnd(-ac),rnd(-ac)),20).

Also, with a HP cap, tough monsters could be made to do meaningful damage.

>* Some small tweaks, like speed boosts for dragons.

A more advanced approach could be to disconnnect movement and attack
speeds. Some monsters would need tweaked (eg air elementals damage was
halved because of their high speed and would need changed back again).

Other ideas;

Implement attacks of opportunity. If the player is next to a monster and
moves away from it and the monster has not attacked him in the time he's
been next to it and the player has taken a time-consuming action while
next to the monster... it gets a (chance (based on how close it is to
getting a move anyway?) of a?) hit on the player.

Cut down on to-hit bonuses so the player can't hit all the time. Give
monsters an AC bonus based on their HD (with a base AC tweak for low-
level monsters so ants don't become invulnerable). Give monsters damage
reduction. Let excess player to-hit reduce monster damage reduction, so that
additional to-hit bonuses are always meaningful. Let monsters burn through
player damage reduction in a similar fashion to make it less valuable.

Do something about twoweaponing. In particular, make it impossible for
multiple weapon or ranged attacks to stack damage bonuses - no matter how
many hits you score, you get one silver bonus, one enchantment damage
bonus, one Strength bonus, etc.
